## Defining Generic Structs

```xiom
pub type Pair[T] = {
  first: T;
  second: T;
}

let p = Pair[Int]{ first: 1, second: 2 };
let q = Pair[Str]{ first: "a", second: "b" };
```

### Multiple Type Parameters
```xiom
pub type Entry[K, V] = {
  key: K;
  value: V;
}

let e = Entry[Str, Int]{ key: "age", value: 30 };
```

### Generic Structs with Constraints
```xiom
pub type SortedPair[T: Ord] = {
  smaller: T;
  larger: T;
}
  invariant: self.smaller <= self.larger;
```

### Generic Struct Methods
```xiom
impl Pair[T] {
  fn swap(self: &Self) -> Pair[T] {
    return Pair[T]{ first: self.second, second: self.first };
  }

  fn map[U](self: &Self, f: fn(T) -> U) -> Pair[U] {
    return Pair[U]{ first: f(self.first), second: f(self.second) };
  }
}
```

### Nested Generics
```xiom
pub type Matrix[T] = Vec[Vec[T]];

pub type Graph[N, E] = {
  nodes: Vec[N];
  edges: Vec[(Int, Int, E)];  // (from, to, edge_data)
}
```

